bootstrap
  Work in your own worktree and confirm it is clean before you edit:
    git status --short
  Bind the lease so the guard can grade your writes, from inside that worktree:
    magus session lease {{.ID}}
  Record the base you landed on; the guard denies every write until the lease has one:
    magus vcs checkpoint -o name
  and register what it prints on lease {{.ID}} with the magus_ledger tool (op register).

rules
  Version control belongs to the orchestrator. Do not commit, push, stash, reset,
  clean, or run `git checkout .`; leave the tree for it to land.
  Write only inside the owned paths above. A path another live lease owns is denied,
  and a path this lease declared forbidden is denied.
  Run the validation above and nothing wider. Never `magus affected ci`.
  Report what you changed, what you verified, and what you left out.

skills to load
  magus-run, before any build, test, lint, or generate.
  magus-vcs-hygiene, before reading a diff or staging anything.
  magus-architecture, before creating a package or a file.
  idiomatic-code-comments, before writing a comment.
